verses.tf_en:
① **«یٰۤاَیُّهَا الَّذِیْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوْا عَدُوِّیْ وَعَدُوَّكُمْ اَوْلِیَاۤءَ تُلْقُوْنَ اِلَیْهِمْ بِالْمَوَدَّةِ»** (O People who Believe! Do not befriend My and your enemy – you reveal secrets to them out of friendship) — *Occasion of Revelation (Sabab an-Nuzul):* On the eve of the historic Conquest of Makkah, the noble Companion Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah (radiyallahu 'anhu)—overwhelmed by human anxiety for the vulnerability of his children and family residing unprotected in Makkah—secretly dispatched a clandestine letter to the Quraish warning them of the Holy Prophet's ﷺ imminent military mobilization. Informed immediately by divine revelation, the Holy Prophet ﷺ dispatched 'Ali, az-Zubayr, and al-Miqdad (radiyallahu 'anhum) who intercepted the courier and retrieved the dispatch. Thereupon, Allah revealed this solemn warning: O believers! Do not take My enemies and your enemies (the belligerent polytheists) as intimate allies and protectors, disclosing confidential military intelligence to them out of personal affection;
② **«وَقَدْ كَفَرُوْا بِمَا جَاۤءَكُمْ مِّنَ الْحَقِّ یُخْرِجُوْنَ الرَّسُوْلَ وَاِیَّاكُمْ اَنْ تُؤْمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ رَبِّكُمْ»** (Whereas they disbelieve in the truth which has come to you! It is they who remove the Noble Messenger and you from your homes, upon your believing in Allah, your Lord;) — Whereas they have brazenly rejected the supreme Truth (the Holy Qur'an and Islam) that has reached you; and they have actively expelled the Noble Messenger ﷺ and driven you out of your ancestral homeland for no other reason than your unwavering faith in Allah, your Cherishing Lord!;
③ **«اِنْ كُنْتُمْ خَرَجْتُمْ جِهَادًا فِیْ سَبِیْلِیْ وَابْتِغَاۤءَ مَرْضَاتِیْ»** (If you have come out to fight for My cause, and to gain My pleasure, then do not befriend them;) — If your migration and military mobilization were truly undertaken to strive in My cause (*Jihad fi Sabeelillah*) and to seek My celestial pleasure (*Ibtigha'a Mardati*), then never compromise that divine mission through covert alliances with the enemies of the faith;
④ **«تُسِرُّونَ إِلَیْهِم بِالْمَوَدَّةِ وَأَنَا۠ أَعْلَمُ بِمَاۤ أَخْفَیْتُمْ وَمَاۤ أَعْلَنتُمْ ۚ وَمَن یَفْعَلْهُ مِنكُمْ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ سَوَاۤءَ السَّبِیلِ»** (You send them secret messages of friendship – and I well know all what you hide and all what you disclose; and whoever among you does it, has indeed strayed away from the right path.) — You transmit clandestine messages of affectionate reassurance to them, whereas I possess all-encompassing knowledge of whatever you conceal in secret and whatever you manifest in the open; and whoever among you engages in such treasonous intrigue has indeed deviated from the straight and secure path of upright faith!

① **«اِنْ یَّثْقَفُوْكُمْ یَكُوْنُوْا لَكُمْ اَعْدَاۤءً»** (If they gain dominance over you they will be your enemies,) — The belligerent disbelievers harbor an incurable, virulent hatred in their hearts; if they ever overcome you, overpower you, or gain military vantage over you, they will instantly display their unmasked, bloodthirsty enmity without mercy;
② **«وَّیَبْسُطُوْۤا اِلَیْكُمْ اَیْدِیَهُمْ وَاَلْسِنَتَهُمْ بِالسُّوْۤءِ»** (And will extend their hands and their tongues towards you with evil,) — And they will stretch out their hands against you with slaughter, plunder, torture, and captivity, and unleash their tongues against you with vile curses, venomous blasphemies, and slanderous abuses;
③ **«وَوَدُّوْا لَوْ تَكْفُرُوْنَ»** (And they wish that in some way you turn disbelievers.) — And their deepest, most desperate desire is that you should somehow renounce your pristine faith and relapse into their darkness of disbelief and idolatry.

① **«قَدْ كَانَتْ لَكُمْ اُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ فِیْۤ اِبْرٰهِیْمَ وَالَّذِیْنَ مَعَهٗ»** (Indeed in Ibrahim, and those along with him, lay a good example for you to follow –) — Truly, there has been for you an illustrious, sublime paradigm to emulate in Prophet Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and the faithful believers who stood with him (such as Prophet Lut and his companions);
② **«اِذْ قَالُوْا لِقَوْمِهِمْ اِنَّا بُرَءٰۤؤُا مِنْكُمْ وَمِمَّا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ كَفَرْنَا بِكُمْ»** (When they said to their people, “Indeed we are unconcerned with you and all what you worship besides Allah; we reject you,) — When they boldly declared unto their idolatrous nation: 'We are wholly disassociated, free, and quit of you and of all the false idols and deities that you worship alongside Allah; we completely renounce and repudiate your false religion;
③ **«وَبَدَا بَیْنَنَا وَبَیْنَكُمُ الْعَدَاوَةُ وَالْبَغْضَاۤءُ اَبَدًا حَتّٰی تُؤْمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَحْدَهٗۤ»** (And between us and you has surfaced enmity and hatred for ever until you accept faith in the One Allah” –) — And there has arisen between us and you open enmity and spiritual aversion forever, until you believe wholeheartedly and exclusively in Allah alone!'—this embodies the timeless foundation of Islamic loyalty and disavowal (*al-Wala' wal-Bara'*), prioritizing loyalty to God above all bloodlines;
④ **«اِلَّا قَوْلَ اِبْرٰهِیْمَ لِاَبِیْهِ لَاَسْتَغْفِرَنَّ لَكَ وَمَاۤ اَمْلِكُ لَكَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَیْءٍ»** (Except the saying of Ibrahim to his father, “I will surely seek forgiveness for you, and I do not possess any power to benefit you against Allah”;) — Except that the promise of Ibrahim to his idolatrous uncle/guardian Azar—saying: 'I will surely pray for your forgiveness, though I have no power to shield you against the decree of Allah'—is not an example for believers to pray for deceased disbelievers; for that was merely a provisional promise Ibrahim gave before it became clear that Azar was an intractable enemy of Allah, after which Ibrahim completely disowned him;
⑤ **«رَبَّنَا عَلَیْكَ تَوَكَّلْنَا وَاِلَیْكَ اَنَبْنَا وَاِلَیْكَ الْمَصِیْرُ»** (“O our Lord! We have relied only upon You, and towards You only we have inclined and only towards You is the return”.) — They suppliantly prayed: 'O our Lord! In You alone have we placed our ultimate trust and reliance (*Tawakkul*), unto You alone have we turned in sincere repentance, and unto Your august presence is the final return of all creation!'

① **«یٰۤاَیُّهَا الَّذِیْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا جَاۤءَكُمُ الْمُؤْمِنٰتُ مُهٰجِرٰتٍ فَامْتَحِنُوْهُنَّ اَللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِاِیْمَانِهِنَّ»** (O People who Believe! When Muslim women leave the lands of disbelief and migrate towards you, examine them; Allah knows more about their faith;) — When the Treaty of al-Hudaybiyyah was ratified, the pagans demanded the return of anyone fleeing to Madinah. While this applied to men, Allah legislated an exemption for female believers: O you who believe! When believing women flee the territory of disbelief (*Dar al-Kufr*) and arrive as emigrants in Madinah, examine their motives under oath—ensuring that they migrated purely out of sincere love for Allah and His Messenger ﷺ, and not out of mere domestic discord or economic incentive; though the innermost truth of their faith is fully known to Allah alone;
② **«فَاِنْ عَلِمْتُمُوْهُنَّ مُؤْمِنٰتٍ فَلَا تَرْجِعُوْهُنَّ اِلَی الْكُفَّارِ لَا هُنَّ حِلٌّ لَّهُمْ وَلَا هُمْ یَحِلُّوْنَ لَهُنَّ»** (So if you judge the women to be believers, do not send them back to the disbelievers; neither are they lawful for the disbelievers, nor are the disbelievers lawful for them;) — Then, if your examination confirms their sincere faith, never return them to their disbelieving husbands in Makkah! For faith has dissolved that marital bond: believing women are strictly unlawful for disbelieving men, nor are disbelieving men lawful husbands for them;
③ **«وَاٰتُوْهُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْفَقُوْا وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَیْكُمْ اَنْ تَنْكِحُوْهُنَّ اِذَاۤ اٰتَیْتُمُوْهُنَّ اُجُوْرَهُنَّ»** (And give their disbelieving husbands what they had spent; and there is no sin upon you to marry them if you give them their bridal money;) — And refund to their disbelieving former husbands the exact dower (*Mahr*) they had originally spent upon them, as fair legal compensation; and there is no sin or impediment for Muslim men to marry these migrant women, provided their waiting period (*'Iddah*) has expired and you pay them their proper bridal dowers;
④ **«وَلَا تُمْسِكُوْا بِعِصَمِ الْكَوَافِرِ وَسَْٔلُوْا مَاۤ اَنْفَقْتُمْ وَلْیَسَْٔلُوْا مَاۤ اَنْفَقُوْا»** (And do not continue the marriage with disbelieving women – and ask for what you had spent, and the disbelievers may ask for what they had spent;) — And do not retain the marital bonds with idolatrous women who remain in disbelief and refuse to emigrate (such marriages stand annulled); and demand back from the pagans the dowers you spent on your wives who apostatized and joined them, just as the disbelievers are entitled to request the dowers they spent on women who joined the Muslims;
⑤ **«ذٰلِكُمْ حُكْمُ اللّٰهِ یَحْكُمُ بَیْنَكُمْ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِیْمٌ حَكِیْمٌ»** (This is Allah’s command; He judges between you; and Allah is All Knowing, Wise.) — This is the binding decree of Allah; He judges between you with consummate equity, wisdom, and justice; and Allah is All-Knowing (*'Aleem*), All-Wise (*Hakeem*).

verses.tf_bn:
① **«یٰۤاَیُّهَا النَّبِیُّ اِذَا جَاۤءَكَ الْمُؤْمِنٰتُ یُبَایِعْنَكَ عَلٰۤی اَنْ لَّا یُشْرِكْنَ بِاللّٰهِ شَیْئًا»** — হে সম্মানিত নবি ﷺ! যখন মুমিন নারীরা আপনার দরবারে উপস্থিত হয়ে এই শর্তে আনুগত্যের বায়আত গ্রহণ করতে চায় যে, তারা মহান আল্লাহর সাথে বিন্দুমাত্র কাউকে শরিক করবে না;
② **«وَّلَا یَسْرِقْنَ وَلَا یَزْنِیْنَ وَلَا یَقْتُلْنَ اَوْلَادَهُنَّ»** — এবং তারা কখনো চুরি করবে না, ব্যভিচার ও অনৈতিক সম্পর্কে লিপ্ত হবে না এবং অজ্ঞতা যুগের মতো দারিদ্র্য বা লজ্জার ভয়ে কন্যা-সন্তানকে জীবন্ত কবর দেবে না বা হত্যা করবে না;
③ **«وَلَا یَاْتِیْنَ بِبُهْتَانٍ یَّفْتَرِیْنَهٗ بَیْنَ اَیْدِیْهِنَّ وَاَرْجُلِهِنَّ»** — এবং এমন কোনো চরম অপবাদ বা মিথ্যা রচনা করবে না যা তারা নিজেদের হাত ও পায়ের মধ্যবর্তী স্থান (অর্থাৎ সন্তান প্রসব ও গর্ভধারণের ক্ষেত্র) নিয়ে উদ্ভাবন করে—যার অর্থ পরপুরুষের সন্তানকে স্বামীর সন্তান বলে দাবি করা অথবা অন্যের ওপর মিথ্যা ব্যভিচারের অপবাদ রটানো;
④ **«وَلَا یَعْصِیْنَكَ فِیْ مَعْرُوْفٍ فَبَایِعْهُنَّ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُنَّ اللّٰهَ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِیْمٌ»** — এবং শরিয়তের কোনো কল্যাণকর ও সৎ নির্দেশে কস্মিনকালেও আপনার অবাধ্য হবে না; তবে আপনি সন্তুষ্টচিত্তে তাদের বায়আত গ্রহণ করুন এবং তাদের অতীত পাপ মোচনের জন্য আল্লাহর নিকট বিশেষভাবে মাগফিরাত প্রার্থনা করুন। নিশ্চয় আল্লাহ পরম ক্ষমাশীল ও অসীম দয়াময়। (হাদিস শরিফে বর্ণিত আছে, রাসুলুল্লাহ ﷺ নারীদের থেকে মৌখিকভাবে বায়আত নিতেন, কোনো পরনারীর হাত স্পর্শ করেননি)।

verses.tf_en:
① **«یٰۤاَیُّهَا النَّبِیُّ اِذَا جَاۤءَكَ الْمُؤْمِنٰتُ یُبَایِعْنَكَ عَلٰۤی اَنْ لَّا یُشْرِكْنَ بِاللّٰهِ شَیْئًا»** (O dear Prophet (Mohammed – peace and blessings be upon him)! If Muslim women come humbly to you to take oath of allegiance at your hands, that they will not ascribe any partner to Allah,) — O Holy Prophet ﷺ! When believing women come humbly to your presence to pledge their solemn oath of allegiance (*Bai'ah*), swearing that they will never associate any partner whatsoever with Allah in worship or sovereignty;
② **«وَّلَا یَسْرِقْنَ وَلَا یَزْنِیْنَ وَلَا یَقْتُلْنَ اَوْلَادَهُنَّ»** (And they will not steal, and will not commit adultery, and will not kill their children,) — And that they will not steal, nor commit fornication or adultery, nor kill their infant children (as was practiced in pagan Jahiliyyah through female infanticide);
③ **«وَلَا یَاْتِیْنَ بِبُهْتَانٍ یَّفْتَرِیْنَهٗ بَیْنَ اَیْدِیْهِنَّ وَاَرْجُلِهِنَّ»** (And will not bring the slander which they fabricate between their hands and feet,) — And that they will not fabricate slander concerning what lies between their hands and feet—which means attributing another man's child to their husband, or inventing false accusations of illicit conduct against innocent persons;
④ **«وَلَا یَعْصِیْنَكَ فِیْ مَعْرُوْفٍ فَبَایِعْهُنَّ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُنَّ اللّٰهَ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِیْمٌ»** (And will not disobey you in any good – then accept their allegiance and seek forgiveness from Allah for them; indeed Allah is Oft Forgiving, Most Merciful.) — And that they will never disobey you in any righteous, virtuous command (*Ma'roof*) of the Sacred Law—then graciously accept their oath of allegiance and supplicate to Allah for their forgiveness! For Allah is indeed Most-Forgiving (*Ghafoor*), Ever-Merciful (*Raheem*). [The noble Sunnah records that the Holy Prophet ﷺ accepted the women's Bai'ah purely verbally, without ever touching the hand of any non-mahram woman].
